    "body": "First bad merge: `6c164521f` (#3790, one ring set). Its parent `df899f029` gives 3 rapid findings. #3790 gives 12. #3777 only renamed the finding: the same 12 moves show before it. #3818 changed the count to 9. All findings are vertical rapids where the shank of the 10 mm flute stands in the part wall. They are real contacts and they hold the post. A 25 mm flute gives no contact finding on the same path. Thus the issue stays P2, not P1. The proof is in `docs/decisions/3811-flute-reach-rapid-reading.md`.\n\nfix on issue/3811-flute-reach · PR #3827 · pinned by a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings, a_twenty_five_mm_flute_gets_no_flute_finding · merges when reviewed",
